# Build output
bin/
obj/
/packages/
*.nupkg

# Test results and coverage
TestResults/
*.trx
coverage*.json
coverage*.xml
*.coverage

# User-specific IDE files
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs
*.DotSettings.user
riderModule.iml
/_ReSharper.Caches/
.vs/
.vscode/

# Rider keeps shared settings in .idea and ignores its own user-specific files there
.idea/**/workspace.xml
.idea/**/shelf/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Renders of content models, made by `sdf render`
content/**/*.png
# ...but the story's screen sources are hand-made inputs (game screenshots, cover art) that StoryScreens turns into the monitor pictures
!content/story/*.png

# Meshes of content models, made by `sdf mesh`
content/**/*.glb

# Unity: files the pipeline and the editor builders regenerate (sdf unity, then Unity's MushroomBuilder / LevelBuilder). Their .meta
# files go with them, as Unity imports them anew; folder .meta files, prefabs, scenes and materials stay in the repo.
# Models meshed by `sdf unity` / `sdf mesh --into`, with suffixed variants (_512, _fast)
Unity/Assets/Mushrooms/Generated/**/*.glb
Unity/Assets/Mushrooms/Generated/**/*.glb.meta
Unity/Assets/Mushrooms/Generated/**/*.json
Unity/Assets/Mushrooms/Generated/**/*.json.meta
# Mesh assets MushroomBuilder writes for the prefabs
Unity/Assets/Mushrooms/Meshes/**/*.asset
Unity/Assets/Mushrooms/Meshes/**/*.asset.meta
# Level bake of `sdf level`: chunks, region maps, instances, level.json
Unity/Assets/Level/Generated/**/*.glb
Unity/Assets/Level/Generated/**/*.glb.meta
Unity/Assets/Level/Generated/**/*.json
Unity/Assets/Level/Generated/**/*.json.meta
Unity/Assets/Level/Generated/**/*.png
Unity/Assets/Level/Generated/**/*.png.meta
Unity/Assets/Level/Generated/**/*.bin
Unity/Assets/Level/Generated/**/*.bin.meta
# Scene backups Unity saves after a crash
Unity/Assets/_Recovery/
Unity/Assets/_Recovery.meta
# Mesh assets and instance data LevelBuilder writes for the level scenes (incl. Mirrored/)
Unity/Assets/Level/Meshes/**/*.asset
Unity/Assets/Level/Meshes/**/*.asset.meta
Unity/Assets/Level/Meshes/**/*.bytes
Unity/Assets/Level/Meshes/**/*.bytes.meta

# Frames of the preview videos (Media/Video/<size>/clipN/*.png) the SDF Media recorder writes; the mp4s and covers are kept
Media/Video/
